================ FINAL SUMMARY ================
Target: race contrast with factor = -0.9568 for BA DEGREE COMPLETED.

MAIN SEARCH (logit, 32 covariate subsets x 3 refs + race-only + per-sex +
pairwise + cloglog/probit/Poisson-log-link + cross-tab ORs):
  Best: Hispanic vs White  | logit race+SEX  | -0.9284 (dev 0.0284) OR 0.3952
        Hispanic vs White  | logit race-only| -0.9241 (dev 0.0327) OR 0.3969
        Black vs White     | logit race-only| -1.0057 (dev 0.0489) OR 0.3658
  No match within 1e-2.

TIE-BREAK ROUND (outputs/tie_break.csv, outputs/tie_break.py):
1. race x SEX interactions: contrasts at Male/Female: Hispanic vs White
   -0.9254/-0.9349 (dev 0.031/0.022); Black vs White -1.0095/-0.9038
   (dev 0.053) — no match.
2. race x SES interactions (SES centered, ref=White): conditional contrasts
   Hispanic vs White: @meanSES -0.7365, @SES-1sd -0.9535 (dev 0.0033),
   @SES+1sd -0.5195; Black vs White: @meanSES -0.9637 (dev 0.0069),
   @SES-1sd -1.0861, @SES+1sd -0.8412. Two conditional values land near the
   target but for DIFFERENT pairs; conditional-on-covariate contrasts are not
   a defensible source specification.
3. Percentile reversed (100-x): race coefficients invariant (linear
   transform) — confirmed numerically, no change.
4. SES quartiles (and SESq + ASVAB z): no match (best dev 0.10+).
5. Subsamples (drop pct<1/>99, pct<5/>95, |SES|>2/2.5sd, fam size 12,
   ASVAB<=1050, CASE ID<=10000): no match within 1e-2; Hispanic vs White
   best -0.9269/-0.9418/-0.9767; Black vs White best -0.9866/-0.9874.
6. L2-penalized logit (sklearn-style objective, Newton solver verified
   against unpenalized MLE): Black-vs-White moves from -1.0057 (C->inf)
   toward 0 and CROSSES -0.9568 at some C in (1,10) — but the required C is
   arbitrary (tuned post hoc); at sklearn default C=1: Black -0.9253,
   Hispanic -0.8158 (neither matches). Hispanic-vs-White moves AWAY from the
   target under shrinkage and can never equal -0.9568 on the penalized path.
   Hence L2 regularization could in principle flip the ranking to
   Black vs White, but only with an unjustifiable penalty choice.
7. BA-as-predictor race models (logit of race A vs B with BA + covariates):
   mirrors the BA-outcome results (identical without covariates; +SEX
   Hispanic vs White -0.9284, race-only -0.9241, Black vs White -1.0057) —
   no match.

MATCHES WITHIN 1e-3: NONE. WITHIN 1e-2: none in the main search; only the
two conditional interaction contrasts (0.0033, 0.0069) fall in (1e-3, 1e-2)
and they point to different pairs.

FINAL DECISION (per protocol): Hispanic vs White, White as reference —
logit coefficient -0.92/-0.93 (OR 0.397) vs target -0.9568 (OR 0.384);
residual ~0.03 log-odds disclosed. Runner-up: Black vs White (-1.006,
OR 0.366); only reachable at the target value via arbitrary L2 penalty
tuning or conditional interaction contrasts.
Sign alignment: negative factor => named race lower odds of BA completion
than White; consistent with raw rates (Hispanic 1.44%, Black 1.33%,
White 3.54%).
